From c9e83fcf0ad0c165650ac077c121cc1c60385e86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:39:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: Report a failed negotiation as a flow error

When pushing a buffer returns GST_FLOW_NOT_NEGOTIATED and no source pad
requests a reconfiguration, the task is stopped and the camera stopped,
but no error is posted on the bus. The pipeline then stays in the
PLAYING state with no data flowing and no indication of the failure to
the application. Post the flow error before stopping the task, as is
done for the other flow errors.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Daniel Golle <daniel@makrotopia.org>
---
 src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
+++ b/src/gstreamer/gstlibcamerasrc.cpp
@@ -419,8 +419,10 @@ int GstLibcameraSrcState::processRequest
 		}
 
 		/* If no pads need a reconfiguration something went wrong. */
-		if (!reconfigure)
+		if (!reconfigure) {
+			GST_ELEMENT_FLOW_ERROR(src_, ret);
 			err = -EPIPE;
+		}
 
 		break;
 	}
